--- TX POWER RF PROOF (AP-side txpower steps, STA-side RSSI, 1472B pings each step) ---
[baseline]        signal: -2 dBm   loss: 0%
[iw set txpower fixed 2000 (20 dBm)] signal: -2 dBm   loss: 0%
[iw set txpower fixed 300 (3 dBm)]  signal: -7 dBm   loss: 0%   <-- RSSI DROPS
[iw set txpower fixed 2000 again]   signal: -2 dBm   loss: 0%   <-- REVERSIBLE
[iw set txpower auto]               signal: -2 dBm   loss: 0%

Interpretation: user dBm settings reach the RF chain (measurable, reversible RSSI response,
zero disruption to the link). Dongles are co-located on one USB hub -> near-field receiver
saturation compresses the observed delta (-2 -> -7 for a 17 dB step); exact dBm accuracy
requires physical separation or a power meter. Readback stays broken (see BUG-08).

--- BUG-08 (upstream mt76 quirk, root-caused this phase) ---
iw dev wlan1 info ALWAYS reports "txpower 3.00 dBm" regardless of settings.
Root cause: mt76_get_txpower() reports DIV_ROUND_UP(phy->txpower_cur + delta, 2), but
NOTHING in the mt7921/connac path ever writes phy->txpower_cur (it stays 0; the 3.00 dBm
is 0 + 2-chain path delta 6 half-dB). All sibling drivers maintain it after programming
rate power (mt7615/mcu.c:2075, mt7996/mcu.c:5352, mt7915/mcu.c:3390) — mt7921 forgot.
Write path is upstream-complete: iw set txpower -> mac80211 conf.power_level ->
mt7921_config(IEEE80211_CONF_CHANGE_POWER) -> mt7921_set_tx_sar_pwr ->
mt76_connac_mcu_set_rate_txpower -> per-channel MCU_CE_CMD(SET_RATE_TX_POWER) batches.

